+## Change: unroll `all()`/`any()` over comprehensions
+
+I teach the assertion rewriter in `src/_pytest/assertion/rewrite.py` to detect calls of the form `all(<comp>)` / `any(<comp>)` where `<comp>` is a generator/list/set comprehension with a single `for` clause and a plain name target. Such a call is rewritten into a `for` loop that short-circuits (like the builtin) but keeps the failing element's value bound, so the explanation reuses the existing machinery and produces a `+ where ...` line instead of `all(<generator object ...>)`.
